\title{RSProtocol: Abstract Base Class for Method Contracts}
\description{
\code{RSProtocol} is the base class for defining behavioral contracts within the RS framework.
Similar to Objective-C's \verb{@protocol}, it specifies method names that a conforming object
is expected to implement.

This class enforces singleton usage: instantiation via \verb{$new()} is blocked if
an instance already exists. Use the class method \verb{$protocol()} instead.

Protocol instances are locked after registration to prevent accidental changes to
the expected method definitions. This immutability ensures that protocol contracts
remain consistent throughout runtime and cannot be redefined dynamically.

Subclasses should override \code{requiredMethods()} to return the character vector of method names.
}
